  "lineage": "Oral epic of the Bani Hilal tribe's migration from Arabia to North Africa, sung by professional poet-singers (sha'ir) of Upper Egypt and the Nile Delta who accompany themselves on the two-string rababa spike fiddle or a frame drum, in performances that can run over many nights. UNESCO proclaimed it a Masterpiece in 2003 and inscribed it in 2008; the rebaba card stands in for the Egyptian two-string rababa.",
